# Catalogue content

Author definitions as JSON documents (one file per entity):

- Tactics → `src/server/content/cards/<card-id>.json`
- Creatures → `src/server/content/creatures/<creature-id>.json`
- Faces → `src/server/content/faces/<face-id>.json`
- Builtin loadouts → `src/server/content/loadouts/<archetype>.json`

Id constants and loaders stay in `cards.ts` / `creatures.ts` / `faces.ts`.
Effects use the AST (`op` nodes) or legacy `type` members compiled by `AstCompiler`.

Rules:

- `rulesText` / print fields are player-facing authority for the UI and use
  [`docs/KEYWORDS.md`](docs/KEYWORDS.md): `On roll: [Mark 1 Toxin].`
  Prefer `[Mark N X]` / `[Strip N X]` over a new verb. Unique one-offs stay
  spelled until a second card needs the same body.
- Structured regions (`effect`, `equipment`, `overload`, `ritual`, attack `effect`, face `onRoll`) only when every clause is modelled.
- Ids: `card-<kebab>`, `creature-<kebab>`, `face-natural|synthetic|untyped-<kebab>`, `attack-<creature>-<kebab>`.
- `equipment` / `overload` are main `CardType` values and must match their regions (and vice versa).
- Rituals use main `type: "ritual"` with ritual subtypes (`instant` / `continuous` / `reaction`) and must have a `ritual` region.
- Update `docs/specs/002|003|004-*.md` and `docs/DEFERRED_CATALOGUE.md` when print coverage changes.
- Dual-timing faces use `On roll:` / `On absorb:` print plus keyword clauses;
  see `.cursor/skills/standardize-card-effects/` and `docs/KEYWORDS.md`.
- Synthetic faces are **named specials only**. Never author blank generics
  (`face-synthetic-martial`, `face-synthetic-corruption`, Forged Martial, …).
- Follow `.cursor/skills/author-content/SKILL.md` for full workflows and templates.
- Honor **attribute exclusive mechanics** in `.cursor/skills/author-content/design.md`.
  Do not print another attribute’s signature verb (scry, mill, prevent,
  opponent-die, toxin markers, ally swap, own-die reconstruction, pack feeding).
- Print voice is the **holder**: `you` is the player whose field the card sits on; `opponent` is that player’s opponent (including after a hand-off / opponent-die forge / opponent equip).
- Printed `energyCost: 1` is exceptional and niche. Prefer 2+; the primary 1-Energy play pattern is cost reduction, not 1-drops.
